# Cloudflare Pages _redirects — host-agnostic, applied AFTER Pages Functions
# (middleware) on both premiselabs.co and tortoise.premiselabs.co.
#
# 1) Trailing-slash variants of indexable pages return 404 on Cloudflare
#    Pages (no directory index) — 301 them to the canonical extensionless URL
#    (Google's "Not found (404)" coverage bucket).
# 2) /index.html is the raw asset behind BOTH host roots — 301 to "/" so the
#    middleware root rewrite (company page / product page) owns the URL.
# 3) .html extension variants of non-auth pages duplicate the extensionless
#    canonical — 301 them (docs/self-hosted only; auth pages keep .html
#    because OAuth redirectTo + invite emails reference it directly).

# Trailing-slash → canonical
/privacy/  /privacy  301
/tos/      /tos      301
/license/  /license  301
/dpa/      /dpa      301
/security/ /security 301
/aviso-privacidad/  /aviso-privacidad  301
/docs/     /docs     301
/self-hosted/  /self-hosted  301
/signin/   /signin   301
/signup/   /signup   301
/welcome/  /welcome  301
/invite-accept/  /invite-accept  301

# Raw index asset → host root (middleware rewrites / per host)
/index.html  /  301

# .html extension duplicates (non-auth only)
/docs.html  /docs          301
/self-hosted.html  /self-hosted  301
